Q1: What are the key limitations of traditional MapReduce that make Spark a preferred choice for modern big data processing?
Disk-based processing causes high I/O overhead.
Slow execution for iterative algorithms.
Complex coding model requiring multiple jobs.
No built-in support for real-time processing.
Poor performance for interactive analytics.

Spark Advantages:

In-memory computation
Faster processing (up to 100x in memory)
Easy APIs (DataFrame, SQL, MLlib)
Supports streaming, machine learning, and graph processing.
