Q2: Explain how Spark uses In-Memory Computing to speed up iterative machine learning algorithms compared to disk-based systems.

Spark stores intermediate data in RAM instead of repeatedly writing it to disk. Machine learning algorithms often require multiple iterations over the same dataset.
By keeping data in memory, Spark avoids expensive disk reads/writes, significantly reducing execution time and improving performance.

