Q11: Explain Shuffle during grouping operations.

A shuffle occurs when Spark redistributes data across partitions so that records with the same key are grouped together.

Example:

df.groupBy("department").count()

Spark must move data between executors to bring all rows of the same department together.

Why is it a wide transformation?

Because data moves across partitions and nodes, unlike narrow transformations where data remains within the same partition.
